<title>CANADA: Western Canada fertilizer shipment, inventory-CFI.</title>
<headline>Western Canada fertilizer shipment, inventory-CFI.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Fertilizer Institute on Monday released its shipment and inventory data.</p>
<p>Western Canadian Fertilizer Shipments</p>
<p>	  July to October 1995 vs 1996</p>
<p>Fertilizer	  Prev Yr (95/96) Cur Yr (96/97) Pct Chng</p>
<p>UREA		  401,172 tonnes  434,162 tonnes +8.2</p>
<p>AMMONIUM SULPHATE  33,769	    36,681	  +8.6</p>
<p>AMMONIUM NITRATE   61,579	    66,211	  +7.5</p>
<p>ANHYDROUS AMMONIA 233,798	   215,752	  -7.7</p>
<p>OTHER*		 19,508	     9,943	 -49.0</p>
<p>TOTAL:		749,826	   762,749	  +1.7</p>
<p>Inventories on Oct 31, 1995 vs 1996</p>
<p>Fertilizer	  Oct 31/95	 Oct 31/96</p>
<p>UREA		   50,801 tonnes  107,444 tonnes</p>
<p>AMMONIUM SULPHATE  95,637	    94,391</p>
<p>AMMONIUM NITRATE   26,475	    34,494</p>
<p>ANHYDROUS AMMONIA 117,544	    81,929</p>
<p>OTHER*		  5,330	    99,521</p>
<p>TOTAL:		295,787	   417,779</p>
<p>*Other includes other phosphates, sulphur solutions, elemental sulphur, sulphate and mixed fertilizer materials.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
